198	     * when absent, joined with {@code '|'} (e.g. {@code +61412345678||H-3F5A9C2E}). Because the
199	     * telephone is part of the key, two owners are duplicates only when their WHOLE identity keys
200	     * are equal; two members of the same household (same {@code householdId}) with different
201	     * telephones have different identity keys and are therefore both allowed. The telephone and
202	     * email are already stored in their normalized forms on create, so this composes them directly.
